      "image": null,
      "content": "AI inference architectures suffer from heavy regime fragmentation. In real-world clusters, top models rarely share identical architectures, while runtime inputs fluctuate drastically across batch sizes, sequence lengths, attention sparsity, and Mixture of Experts routing patterns. Handcrafted static kernel optimizations fall short under this variance.\n\nThe Together Compiler addresses this bottleneck through continual compilation, replacing rigid heuristics with an autonomous optimization loop. By treating kernel tuning as a live search space across diverse accelerators such as H100s, B200s, and specialized ASICs, the runtime adapts execution paths to actual traffic shapes without human intervention.\n\nMoving compilation from an ahead-of-time manual ritual into a continual online feedback loop fundamentally alters how we scale high-throughput model serving."
    },
    {
