      "content": "Local-first architectures often force engineers to trade developer ergonomics for consistency. Tandem tackles this by pairing an in-memory, queryable database on the client with an automated background sync engine that requires no specialized synchronization backend.\n\nThe client writes optimistically to its local storage, re-renders the UI immediately, and streams mutation operations to the server. When the server responds, Tandem reconciles conflicts by deterministically replaying outstanding local changes on top of the confirmed state, rolling back invalid operations without dropping user input.\n\nBecause state propagation happens before heavy confirmation round-trips, reads remain instant through IndexedDB caches while maintaining end-to-end data safety.\n\nDesigning synchronization around optimistic logs rather than ad-hoc state diffs eliminates an entire class of race conditions."
