      "content": "Traditional Git servers hit severe bottlenecks when subjected to thousands of concurrent automated pushes from CI jobs and AI agents. Local disk locks and ref contention quickly overwhelm the conventional filesystem layout.\n\nAspen addresses this architectural bottleneck by decoupling Git storage into two specialized layers, adapting concepts from internal systems like OpenAI Pando. It stores packfiles directly in object storage while persisting branch history, commit metadata, and references inside PostgreSQL. The server speaks standard Git over HTTP and SSH, meaning clients require zero modifications while gaining horizontally scalable persistence.\n\nTreating Git storage as an object store backed by relational metadata unlocks resilient high-throughput infrastructure. Decoupling refs from disk structures solves the scaling bottlenecks of agent-driven software development."
